WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.362
Hi! Writing a story is like building with blocks, one piece at a time. Today we'll learn to write a complete short story.

2
00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:16.242
The beginning tells who, when and where: One Saturday morning, Sam went to the park.

3
00:00:16.392 --> 00:00:21.162
The middle tells the problem: Suddenly, his kite got stuck in a tree.

4
00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:25.362
The ending tells how it was solved and how the characters felt.

5
00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:30.210
You can end with one sentence about what was learnt.

6
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:36.042
The story already happened, so use the past tense: went, saw, felt.

7
00:00:36.192 --> 00:00:40.098
Use Suddenly, Soon and Finally to link events.

8
00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:45.546
Show feelings: His heart beat fast is livelier than just saying scared.

9
00:00:45.696 --> 00:00:50.442
Add a line of speech and the story comes alive.

10
00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:56.010
Watch out! The story already happened, so don't use the present tense!

11
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.490
Go becomes went, and is becomes was.

12
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:05.178
After writing, check that every verb is in the past tense.

13
00:01:05.328 --> 00:01:13.626
Your turn! Which part tells who, when and where? Pause and think.

14
00:01:13.776 --> 00:01:19.506
The beginning tells who, when and where. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:19.656 --> 00:01:28.386
Another one! Which word is good for starting a problem? Pause and think.

16
00:01:28.536 --> 00:01:36.258
Suddenly shows something happened unexpectedly, so it starts a problem. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:36.408 --> 00:01:46.626
Here's another! Mei see a lost puppy. In a story, how should see change? Pause and think.

18
00:01:46.776 --> 00:01:53.418
Stories use the past tense, so see becomes saw. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:53.568 --> 00:02:05.418
Try one more! Which sentence shows fear better? A: He was scared. B: His knees shook. Pause and think.

20
00:02:05.568 --> 00:02:11.946
B shows how his body felt, so it's livelier. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:12.096 --> 00:02:19.842
Try one more! Which is a good ending? Pause and think.

22
00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:26.274
B tells how the problem was solved and how they felt. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:26.424 --> 00:02:35.058
Try one more! Which part tells how the problem is solved? Pause and think.

24
00:02:35.208 --> 00:02:42.258
The ending tells how the problem is solved and how the characters feel. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:42.408 --> 00:02:50.514
Last one! Which word is good for the ending? Pause and think.

26
00:02:50.664 --> 00:02:57.450
Finally means at last, so it often starts the ending. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:09.018
Remember: a story has a beginning, middle and ending. Write in the past tense, link events with Suddenly and Finally, and add feelings and speech to make it lively.

28
00:03:09.168 --> 00:03:13.721
Try writing a five-sentence story today!

